/-!
# A derived complete sheaf with locally constant reduction is a quotient of `(Λ̲^∧)^{⊕t}`

Let `X` be a weakly contractible affine scheme, `Λ` a Noetherian ring and `I ⊂ Λ` an ideal. Let `ℱ`
be a derived complete sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `X_proétale` whose reduction `ℱ/Iℱ` is a locally
constant sheaf of `Λ/I`-modules of finite type. Then `ℱ` is a quotient of a finite direct sum of
copies of the completed constant sheaf `Λ̲^∧ = lim (Λ/Iⁿ)̲`. This is [Stacks, Tag 09BZ].

The proof follows the source. Since `X` is weakly contractible, the covering trivializing
`ℱ/Iℱ` is refined by a finite disjoint clopen decomposition of `X` ([Stacks, Tag 098F]); on
each piece `ℱ/Iℱ` is the constant sheaf of a finite `Λ/I`-module, and the generators of these
modules, extended by zero to the other pieces, give finitely many global sections of `ℱ/Iℱ`,
which lift to global sections `s_k` of `ℱ`. Each `s_k` lies in the image of a map `Λ̲^∧ ⟶ ℱ`,
because `ℱ` is derived complete. The cokernel of the resulting map `(Λ̲^∧)^{⊕t} ⟶ ℱ` is then
shown to vanish by derived Nakayama, on the sections over the affine weakly contractible
objects.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.exists_epi_sigma_completedConstantSheaf_of_isDerivedComplete`:
  **[Stacks, Tag 09BZ]**.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.exists_finite_globalSections_locallyGenerating`: a locally constant
  sheaf of finite type on a weakly contractible affine scheme is locally generated by finitely
  many global sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.exists_finite_globalSections_span`: a sheaf of `Λ̲`-modules whose
  underlying sheaf of `Λ`-modules is such a sheaf is generated by finitely many global sections
  over every affine weakly contractible object.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.idealSections_constantCoefficientIdealSheaf_eq`: over an affine
  weakly contractible object, the sections of `IΛ̲` form the ideal generated by `I`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.ProEt.existsUnique_glue_of_isClopenDecompositionCover`: gluing of
  sections along a finite disjoint clopen decomposition.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.epi_of_surjective_sections`: a map of sheaves of `Λ̲`-modules which
  is surjective on the sections over a covering family of objects is an epimorphism.

## Implementation notes

The source obtains the map `Λ̲^∧ ⟶ ℱ` through a section `s` from the derived completion of `Λ̲`,
which it computes by [Stacks, Tag 099M], and shows that the cokernel of `(Λ̲^∧)^{⊕t} ⟶ ℱ` is
derived complete by [Stacks, Tag 099Q] before applying [Stacks, Tag 09BY]. Here the map is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.exists_completedConstantSheaf_hom_of_isDerivedComplete`, which works on
sections, and the vanishing of the cokernel is checked on the sections over each affine weakly
contractible object `W`: evaluation at `W` is exact, the sections of `ℱ` and of `Λ̲^∧` over `W`
are derived complete `Λ`-modules, so the cokernel of the map on sections is derived complete
([Stacks, Tag 091U]), and it vanishes modulo `I` by the choice of the `s_k`, hence vanishes by
derived Nakayama for modules ([Stacks, Tag 09B9]).

A sheaf of `Λ`-modules on `X_proétale` is a sheaf of modules over the constant coefficient ring
sheaf `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.constantCoefficientRingedSite`. Its reduction `ℱ/Iℱ` is the
cokernel of the inclusion of the adic filtration `Iℱ`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealPowerProduct` at exponent one), read as a sheaf of
`Λ`-modules; that it is a locally constant sheaf of `Λ/I`-modules of finite type is the
existence of a sheaf of `Λ/I`-modules which is locally constant with finitely generated values
(`Stacks.ConstantSheaf.IsFiniteTypeLocallyConstant`, the condition of [Stacks, Tag 03RW]) and
whose restriction of scalars to `Λ` is isomorphic to it. The direct sum `(Λ̲^∧)^{⊕t}` is the finite
coproduct in the abelian category of sheaves of modules, and `Λ̲^∧` is the completed constant
sheaf of [Stacks, Tag 093M], read over the constant coefficient ring sheaf.

The coefficient ring is taken in `Type (u + 1)` for `X : Scheme.{u}`, the universe of the
sections of sheaves of modules on `X_proétale`, so that coefficients and sections lie in one
universe, which is where the module-theoretic input
`AdicCompletionFlatTensor.bijective_comp_adicCompletionOf` is available.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09BZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09BZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 098F](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/098F)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099M)
